WEBVTT

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.708
I learned how to disagree
without being disagreeable.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:36.143
I studied evidence that negotiations
hinge on two big priorities:

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:38.184
results and relationships,

00:03:38.208 --> 00:03:39.809
but many people make the mistake

00:03:39.833 --> 00:03:42.083
of focusing on one
and neglecting the other.

00:03:43.125 --> 00:03:45.601
It was so helpful
that when I became a professor,

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:48.226
I signed up to start
teaching negotiations.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.768
My goal was to help students
learn that it's possible

00:03:50.792 --> 00:03:53.917
to get the results they want
without hurting their relationships.

00:03:54.708 --> 00:03:56.768
When Grace walked
into my class at Wharton,

00:03:56.792 --> 00:03:58.708
she reminded me a lot of my former self.

00:03:59.625 --> 00:04:01.309
For as long as she could remember,